you make a dinner reservation, you use formal words and expressions. You can use verbs with infinitives such as <span class=\"italic\">like to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">want to</span>.<br>When you answer people's requests, it is important to reply in a polite way.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Making a Reservation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would like to book a table.<br />I would like to make a reservation.<br>Do you have room for 5 people tomorrow?<br>Could we book a table for Sunday?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Certainly, Sir/Madam.<br>For how many people?<br>Absolutely. Would you like to make a reservation?<br>I'm very sorry, we are closed on Sundays.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I would like to book a table for tomorrow. <br><span class=\"strong\">Waiter</span>: Certainly. For how many people? <br> <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Four people, please. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Waiter</span>: Very well. May I have your name for the reservation, please?  ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "closed ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not open", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The restaurant is closed on Sundays.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you make a dinner reservation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "booked", "type": "name"}, {"content": "full; reserved", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sorry, we are completely booked for dinner tomorrow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to apologize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say sorry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I apologize for the inconvenience.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in case", "type": "name"}, {"content": "if; in the event of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You could make a reservation in case someone cancels.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cancellation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a decision not to go ahead with a reservation or arrangement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have a cancellation. Would you like to book a table?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I'm afraid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I'm sorry; unfortunately ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The restaurant is completely booked, I'm afraid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Call a restaurant to make a reservation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Respond to the reservation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make and respond to the requests in a polite way.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying your dialogue aloud with your partner.